-20\\\",\\\"dateModified\\\":\\\"2026-11-20\\\",\\\"author\\\":{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Organization\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"DigiRobotics Team\\\"},\\\"publisher\\\":{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Organization\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"DigiRobotics\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://digirobotics.xyz\\\"},\\\"mainEntityOfPage\\\":\\\"https://digirobotics.xyz/blog/smart-glasses-and-the-token-economy\\\",\\\"image\\\":\\\"https://digirobotics.xyz/images/blog/smart-glasses-and-the-token-economy-cover.jpg\\\"}\"}}],[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"header\",null,{\"className\":\"relative overflow-hidden border-b border-white/10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"absolute inset-0 opacity-25 [background-image:radial-gradient(oklch(from_var(--primary)_l_c_h_/_24%)_1px,transparent_1px)] [background-size:22px_22px]\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative mx-auto max-w-5xl px-5 pb-16 pt-12 sm:px-8 sm:pb-24 sm:pt-16\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{\"href\":\"/blog\",\"className\":\"inline-flex min-h-11 items-center gap-2 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-[var(--muted-foreground)] transition hover:text-[var(--primary)]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L4\",null,{\"icon\":{\"name\":\"arrow-left\",\"size\":24,\"node\":[[\"path\",{\"d\":\"m12 19-7-7 7-7\",\"key\":\"1l729n\"}],[\"path\",{\"d\":\"M19 12H5\",\"key\":\"x3x0zl\"}]]},\"size\":14,\"aria-hidden\":\"true\"}],\" Back to field notes\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-14 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--primary)]\",\"children\":\"Robotics\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"text-white/25\",\"children\":\"/\"}],[\"$\",\"time\",null,{\"dateTime\":\"2026-11-20\",\"className\":\"text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":\"November 20, 2026\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"text-white/25\",\"children\":\"/\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":\"12 min read\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"h1\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-6 max-w-5xl font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-[-0.03em] text-white\",\"children\":\"Smart Glasses and the Token Economy\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-8 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[var(--muted-foreground)] sm:text-2xl\",\"children\":\"New research shows robots can learn manipulation skills purely from smart glasses video — no robot needed during collection. Combined with audio tokenization advances, first-person experience compresses into discrete, licensable, payable experience tokens — the unit of currency for embodied AI.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-10 flex items-center gap-3 text-[14px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"grid size-10 place-items-center rounded-full border border-[var(--primary)]/40 bg-[var(--primary)]/10 font-heading text-[var(--primary)]\",\"children\":\"DR\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold\",\"children\":\"DigiRobotics Team\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-0.5 text-[12px] text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":[\"Updated \",\"November 20, 2026\"]}]]}]]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-12 px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-24 lg:grid-cols-[170px_minmax(0,760px)] lg:justify-center\",\"children\":[\"$L5\",\"$L6\"]}]]}],\"$L7\"]}],null,\"$L8\"]}],\"isPartial\":\"$@9\",\"staleTime\":\"$a\",\"varyParams\":null},{\"rsc\":\"$Lb\",\"isPartial\":\"$@c\",\"staleTime\":\"$a\",\"varyParams\":null},{\"rsc\":\"$Ld\",\"isPartial\":\"$@e\",\"staleTime\":\"$a\",\"varyParams\":\"$f\"},{\"rsc\":\"$L10\",\"isPartial\":\"$@11\",\"staleTime\":\"$a\",\"varyParams\":\"$f\"}],\"isUpgradeableISRFallback\":false,\"a\":\"$@12\",\"rootVaryParams\":null,\"needsRuntimeRequest\":\"$@13\"}\n1f:I[38437,[\"99489\",\"static/chunks/99489-7b4b74c1a59849db.js\",\"5772\",\"static/chunks/5772-2ad3d6bb0136fa62.js\",\"57304\",\"static/chunks/57304-ca98254065b92130.js\",\"95953\",\"static/chunks/app/blog/%5Bslug%5D/page-a38ec015cb873e3f.js\"],\"Image\"]\n24:I[90484,[],\"OutletBoundary\"]\n25:\"$Sreact.suspense\"\n27:I[90484,[],\"ViewportBoundary\"]\n28:I[90484,[],\"MetadataBoundary\"]\n29:I[86869,[],\"IconMark\"]\n2a:I[57121,[],\"\"]\n2b:I[74581,[],\"\"]\n5:[\"$\",\"aside\",null,{\"className\":\"hidden lg:block\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sticky top-28 border-t border-[var(--primary)] pt-4 font-mono text-[9px] uppercase leading-5 tracking-[0.15em] text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":[\"DigiRobotics\",[\"$\",\"br\",null,{}],\"Field note\",[\"$\",\"br\",null,{}],\"2026.11.20\"]}]}]\n6:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"min-w-0\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"blockquote\",\"blockquote-0\",{\"className\":\"my-10 border-l-2 border-[var(--primary)] bg-[var(--primary)]/[0.06] px-6 py-2 font-heading text-xl leading-8 text-white sm:px-8\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-0\",{\"className\":\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-white\",\"children\":\"TL;DR:\"}]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-1\",{\"className\":\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":\"New open-source research shows robots can learn real manipulation skills from ordinary smart glasses video — zero-shot, with no robot in the loop during collection. Parallel advances in audio tokenization provide the blueprint for compressing continuous human experience into discrete, typed, machine-manipulable experience tokens. Tokenized experience fixes the three problems of raw recordings: granular pricing, machine-readable licensing, and unit-level verification. DigiRobotics is building the marketplace where experience tokens trade — robot-to-contributor or agent-to-agent, with sub-cent stablecoin settlement.\"}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-0\",{\"className\":\"mb-4 mt-6 scroll-mt-24 font-heading text-xl md:text-2xl leading-tight tracking-[-0.03em] text-white\",\"children\":\"Robot Skills from Ordinary Wearables\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-0\",{\"className\":\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":\"A recently released research project demonstrated something deceptively simple: a robot can learn to manipulate objects from nothing but first-person video recorded on consumer smart glasses. A human wears the glasses, performs a task — picking up a slice of bread, placing it on a plate — and the system extracts everything needed to teach a research robot arm the same skill.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-1\",{\"className\":\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":\"The pipeline matters more than the software. Capture happens on commodity wearables — everyday glasses with built-in cameras, not lab rigs, collecting in-the-wild human demonstrations. Automated perception extraction processes first-person video into camera pose, hand trajectories, and 3D hand tracking from the operator's perspective. Geometric grounding uses a handful of labeled object points to turn loose footage into physically meaningful coordinates. And zero-shot transfer means the policy trained purely on human experience executes directly on a robot arm, with no additional robot-side data collection.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-1\",{\"className\":\"mb-4 mt-6 scroll-mt-24 font-heading text-xl md:text-2xl leading-tight tracking-[-0.03em] text-white\",\"children\":\"Experience Becomes Tokens\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-2\",{\"className\":\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":\"The second half of the story comes from a different corner of AI: tokenization. Modern neural audio systems compress continuous sound waves into short sequences of discrete tokens — compact symbols that large language-model architectures can learn from, generate, and trade across systems.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-3\",{\"className\":\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":\"The maturation of this field offers a playbook for embodied data. Compress without losing meaning — encoder-decoder architectures and quantization techniques crush high-dimensional signals into small token streams while preserving what downstream models need. Separate concerns — modern tokenizers split signals into parallel streams: semantic content (what is happening) versus acoustic detail (how it sounds). Physical AI needs the same split — task semantics versus sensor texture. Accept trade-offs consciously — tokenization research explicitly weighs reconstruction fidelity against semantic richness; robotics data will need the same deliberate costing of what details to keep. And enable LLM-style training — discrete tokens let transformer models absorb the medium natively; lessons from audio now apply directly to point sequences, action chunks, and multi-sensor streams from egocentric capture.\"}],\"\\n\",\"$L14\",\"\\n\",\"$L15\",\"\\n\",\"$L16\",\"\\n\",\"$L17\",\"\\n\",\"$L18\",\"\\n\",\"$L19\",\"\\n\",\"$L1a\",\"\\n\",\"$L1b\",\"\\n\",\"$L1c\",\"\\n\",\"$L1d\"],\"$L1e\"]}]\n7:[\"$\",\"footer\",null,{\"className\":\"border-t border-white/[.08] bg-[#111620] py-12\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto w-full max-w-[1440px] px-5 sm:px-8 lg:px-12 xl:px-16\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] lg:items-start\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L1f\",null,{\"src\":\"/digirobotics/brand/digirobotics-logo.png\",\"alt\":\"DigiRobotics.xyz\",\"width\":210,\"height\":48,\"className\":\"h-auto w-[190px]\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-4 text-[17px] text-white/60\",\"children\":\"Egocentric data for robotics training.\"}]]}],[\"$